# Go backend conventions

- Go 1.27, `CGO_ENABLED=0`, module `github.com/bvaliev/brokerium`. Run Go through `mise exec --`.
- First line of every file: `// SPDX-License-Identifier: LicenseRef-PolyForm-Shield-1.0.0`.
- HTTP: standard library `net/http` with method patterns (`mux.HandleFunc("GET /api/v1/...", h)`).
  JSON errors use `{"error": {"code": "...", "message": "..."}}`.
- Logging with `log/slog`; never log credentials, SASL payloads or message contents.
- Pass `context.Context` as the first argument; respect cancellation in loops that talk to Kafka.
- Wrap errors with `fmt.Errorf("doing x: %w", err)`; return typed errors for API-visible cases.
- Kafka access only through `internal/kafka`. Use `kadm` when it covers the feature, `kmsg`
  requests for KRaft-specific APIs. Always check per-partition and per-resource error codes.
- `internal/balancer` stays pure: no I/O, no time, no randomness without an explicit seed.
- Database access through `internal/store` with pgx; schema changes are new numbered files in
  `internal/store/migrations`, never edits of applied migrations.
- Tests: table-driven, `t.Parallel()` where safe, no network in unit tests (`kfake` or fakes);
  integration tests that need the lab use the `e2e` build tag.
